\chapter{On1xMETA rules and partial evaluation}
\label{ch:75}
\index{On1xMETA rules and partial evaluation}
\index{Optimization!On1xMETA}

On1xMETA describes checked transformations and semantic constraints. The build validates rule payloads and compiles them into native compiler code. Definitions have authored source locations that can be reported with rule hits. The bootstrap accepts verified generated inputs according to its own snapshot checks. Emitted programs do not need the parser generator or the rule-generation scripts.

\section{Select and inspect a rule}
Use \OnxCodeTerm{--dump-processor} for the checked input and enabled rules. A neutral arithmetic form can simplify while preserving the traps and effects of its operand. Partial evaluation is a bounded optimization of admitted computation, with residual runtime code when the conditions are insufficient. To test a rule, use matching and nonmatching shapes and a boundary expression whose observable trap or side effect must survive. Report which rule fired, where it came from, and which effective optimization profile permitted it. Source-level PPX operates earlier over another schema.

